  "description": "A Press Core: stamps parts out of extruded pieces. Alone it takes blanks up to 0.45 m across; weld Press Blocks beside it for a bed (its width the widest blank), stack blocks on the bed's long edges for walls (1.6 m of daylight, 2 m more a block), and it works faster with every block. A die in its slot sets what it makes; blanks go in bay 1, a die's kit in bay 2. Needs power.",
